Z||000011||Haze_Performance||02-07-2001||09:44 PM||||Well a I see it...............<P>This is a <B>FREE</B> Forum...NO ONE PAID to join this. Are you being called at your home or work with people asking for money?? Are you getting emails asking to donate?? Are you getting mail delivered to your house?? Is there someone knocking on your door??   <P><B>NO!!!!</B><P>Can we all just get over it? If you dont want to donation then DONT!!! I dont care if he makes $10,000 on the T-Tops. If he gave $5.00 to the ABF, That would be $5.00 more than he had. Thats money that he didnt have to give & he did it to be kind!!!<P><BR>Im done... No hard feelings toward anyone..<P><BR>TFTS   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 02-07-2001).]||||reg||2
Z||000012||84segirl||02-07-2001||09:55 PM||||black88gt, what do you mean? I believe Orge and Gtsonly said it in a very "PC" manner. Haze, you are right, no one has paid a dime to join this forum and it is a forum of free speech. But this situation has gotten a tad out of hand. It is like answering your phone to only hear the voice of a telemarketer trying to sell you something, even though you tell them you are not interested they just keep calling you back and back, every nite, over and over. Wouldn't you , Haze, get tried of it?||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cliff Pennock||02-07-2001||10:06 PM||||Well, I agree and disagree. It's been a point I have been discussing in private email in the past with someone here on the forum.<P>A lot of times an idea is born here -good or bad- which requires funds for whatever reason. When that idea is posted, the responses are mostly positive and <B>a lot</B> of people reply with "great idea! count me in!". But when it's actually time to fork over the money, nobody's home. This has happened a lot in the past now and I can understand it's incredibly frustrating for those who have put a lot of time (and/or money) in realizing the idea.<P>Now I understand there have been (and will be ) more people that have been in some kind of trouble - illness, accidents, whatever, that haven't been helped. This does not mean that it's in any way unfair that we (at least some of us) chose to help someone else - even someone we know nothing about. It's a random act of kindness, something people should do more often. Because I can't help <B>everyone</B> doesn't mean I shouldn't help <B>anyone</B>.<P>If you feel bad/angry because there are some people here that have chosen to help Anthony Barber and you get sick and tired of reading posts about it, there's a simple solution. Skip those topics.<P>Personally, I don't think of anyone being a lesser person if they don't donate anything.<P>But this idea started because we <B>as PFF</B> wanted to make a difference for someone. It turns out we <B>as PFF</B> don't do diddly-squat. It was probably wrong to assume that the voices of a few people would be representative for the whole forum. I guess that's where all this went wrong.<P>So my suggestion to everyone is: chill. If the fund doesn't raise as much as some of us have hoped for - so be it. If some people think we shouldn't be doing this at all, or just the opposite - respect those that think otherwise.<P>But I hope you can all understand that from now on I will cut flame-wars over this short. I haven't been following the Barber threads lately but will do so from now on.||||reg||1
Z||000014||wkayl||02-07-2001||10:15 PM||||I did a search on this topic.  38 people including myself said they would contribute to this fund.  As of this morning only 7 deposits have been made.  That doesn’t count what may be in the mail or posted today.  I won’t know until after 7AM if anything was received today.   Several went the extra mile to get this fund rolling.  You know who you are and thank you.  Everyone bookmark this site if you want to be kept updated. <A HREF="http://www.fierowayne.homestead.com/acount.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierowayne.homestead.com/acount.html</A>  <BR>I will not be making any more posts on this topic.  ||||reg||9
Z||000015||84segirl||02-07-2001||10:17 PM||||To cliff,<BR>  I know I am new to this forum and it is a great forum for all lovers of the fiero. I hope you have not misunderstood what I am trying to say. I think it is great that a person can give of himself in the smallest of matters to help another and I have no problems with that and I hope people feel good enough to help in whatever why they can. Be it money, thought or prayer. But when the deposit records are posted and Statements to accompany those deposit slip posts to the tone of " come on people, you said you were going to send money, where is it?" I feel that has gone beyond being human and help a fellow person. I hope you can see my point of view and not pursecute for it.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Haze_Performance||02-07-2001||10:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 84segirl:<BR><B>Haze, you are right, no one has paid a dime to join this forum and it is a forum of free speech. But this situation has gotten a tad out of hand. It is like answering your phone to only hear the voice of a telemarketer trying to sell you something, even though you tell them you are not interested they just keep calling you back and back, every nite, over and over. Wouldn't you , Haze, get tried of it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>But your NOT being called... You have the choice not to go into a Topic. Also unlike a phone call...the Topic is not directed tword a single person. The reason this is getting out of hand is because people are starting new topics to express there rage about this whole ABF Topic... This is just a stinkin internet chat site (no offence Cliff)...Its not the New York Times.. No one is being forced by gun point to give there money to Anthony...... I feel bad for ANYONE that lives & breaths just to read and post on this website.<P>Lets just get over it.............<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A>||||reg||10
