Z||000022||JohnnyK||02-07-2001||11:37 PM||||Toss the witch out of here? She was saying what lots/most of people were thinking. She said nothing wrong except a little insult to Haze, but his posts were just as offensive to her.||||reg||1
Z||000023||Haze_Performance||02-07-2001||11:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Toss the witch out of here? She was saying what lots/most of people were thinking. She said nothing wrong except a little insult to Haze, but his posts were just as offensive to her.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hey Johnny,<BR>  Where did I insult her? I have NO hard feelings tword anyone about the ABF Topic. As you can see none of my replies were directed tword anyone specific.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Im going to take my own advise & just ignore all the B.S. Topics...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A>||||reg||1
Z||000024||DaRkLoRD||02-08-2001||12:08 AM||||I realize pagans aren't exactly a large religious group anymore, but still, it's hardly justification to use names in a derogatory fashion like that.. this is similar to one of my friends who uses the term jew as an insult.. it never bothered me too much until I became good friends with some people who are jewish. Now I notice things like that a lot more, and it bothers me.. (btw, I have many pagan friends as well, and the stereotypes about them are so twisted it's sickening.)<BR>and yes, I know this has nothing to do with the ABF donation fund topic..<P>btw Tina, aside from all this.. welcome to the forum. we're usually pretty friendly here.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000025||TwisT||02-08-2001||12:10 AM||||My penny's worth of input...<P>Perhaps PFF,  as a whole,  is too young yet for the kind of dedication we'd like to look for in this fund.  Everyone knows how this forum works...  and like a TV...  can choose to tune into,  or not to tune into certain topics (including this one).  But I myself can tell you that enthusiasm for anything,  donation or otherwise,  can easily be transmitted through the keyboard.  Maybe too easily...<P>Good intentions sometimes are exactly that...  meaning,  a person WANTS to do what they can to help.  Following through is a completely different subject.<P>I,  for one,  still love Fieros and love this forum (thanks Cliff).  I may not post nearly as much as a lot of you,  but still read regularly and learn a lot because of it.  <P>People,  please understand that behind these words you see on your computer screen,  there are human beings.  We're not perfect.  We make mistakes.  But I believe all of our intentions are real.<P>Happy Fiero-ing!<P>Brett<BR>'88 "ITALFIERO" GT      <p>[This message has been edited by TwisT (edited 02-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000026||RaeQwan||02-08-2001||12:13 AM||||I will most defintly throw my word in here, just to add to what Haze said, this is a free forum yes, and no its not like picking up the phone to a telemarketer... for the fact, you are not forced to click on the link to a thread. its a choice done freely, and if anyone is threatening you into doing it, You need to tell Mr. Giggles to eat some cheese. Since when has ppl begged for money?<P>oh please please send me money so I can paint my car again please please.. not my best begging but that is your example of begging. Seeing as how this has quickly bored me, I'm done.<P>------------------<BR>Ray - AIM: WookieeNC<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ray19nc/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Fiero Coupe</A> - <A HREF="http://www.CarolinaFieros.com" TARGET=_blank>Carolina Fieros</A> - <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/dearabu/" TARGET=_blank>Dear Abu</A> - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.net" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Network</A>||||reg||1
Z||000027||stimpy||02-08-2001||12:28 AM||||I'm conflicted on this issue.  On one hand I look at the fact that we have a person who is in need.  Individuals felt that it would be appropriate to tender some kind of support for this stranger in a good Samaritan manner.  I'm all for that. The family set up an account of their own to receive donations for this purpose. Then a groundswell of enthusiasm arises on how <B>neat</B> it would be to replace this guys car. {Side note- Having worked in rehab hospitals I can attest that there are far more pressing needs for someone with head trauma and some degree of brain damage then a fly car.} So one man took it upon himself to create a fund for this purpose.  Mr. Kayl, do you know the meaning yet of "No good deed goes unpunished"?<P>I suppose my unvarnished opinion of this whole state of events is this. While the whole PFF ABF is a bit self-serving, there are still 31 people out there who pledged their support. It's time for them to put up or shut up.  Those who avoided making that pledge, I certainly don't feel that you should be made to feel guilty.   ||||reg||1
Z||000028||stimpy||02-08-2001||12:30 AM||||Oh, and segirl, please don't average out my post-per-day. I already know that I don't have a life.||||reg||1
Z||000029||Neverfinished||02-08-2001||12:35 AM||||Do any of you think Antonhy would really like a bunch of people fighting over him. I don't even know the guy and I give out my deepest sympathy. I have had 3 friends die in car accidents in the past 2 years and I know how it feels to hurt for someone. But PLEASE end this Shi*! I don't know if you guys are undersexed or something but grow up and stop bickering. If anyone replys to my post do so in a well suited manner. Get a life and stop bitching about peoples beliefs. I am only talking of course to the guys who won't stop stressing their point about how they're just trying to do the right thing. Give it up. <BR>Feel free to pick apart my post all you want and I am on segirls side all the way. SEgirl feel free to e-mail me anytime you want.<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
