Z||000031||Haze_Performance||02-08-2001||12:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>Hey, I live and breath just to post and read this site   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Shhhh.... dont tell anyone...but so do I  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A>||||reg||14
Z||000032||Cliff Pennock||02-08-2001||06:02 AM||||My last words on this and then I'll shut up. I just checked how many posts were actually spend on this whole fund deal. And to be honest I haven't got a ****ing clue where people get the idea anything is being forced upon them. Buried within the 300,000 messages are a few posts asking to help out a fellow Fiero owner. There are almost 2000 members on this forum. I bet 1500+ don't even know who Anthony Barber is. 84segirl, you think that posting something like "come on people, you said you were going to send money, where is it?" is out of line? Well, I don't believe it is. Because some people have spent a lot of time setting this up because of those statements. They have even talked to the family and said "we represent a great group of people on the internet and we have decided to show our support". Yeah, a whole whopping 0.05% of that group. I <B>know</B> I am out of line here saying this, because my words possibly carry a little more weight than those of others but I'm a bit disappointed in all this. I read the messages every day: "thanks, the forum has saved me tons of money", "thanks for providing this service for free". Now something is asked in return and people start weighing the pros and cons of donating a few bucks. I think PFF has lost face big time.<P>My apologies for saying this (and it's with great hesitation that I do) - but it's damn hard for me not always being able to speak my opinion and have to try to be PC about everything...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000033||Old Lar||02-08-2001||06:04 AM||||It goes to show that no good deed goes unpunished!<P>Thanks for the work wkayl.||||reg||1
Z||000034||BAM-BAM||02-08-2001||08:17 AM||||  Ok, for the record. There has never been anyone asking for money since the conception of this idea. There was a statement urging those whose initialy stepped up to come forward. Since then it has been the sceptics that have kept this going. Those people who are obviously so devoid of comon sense that they can't see the forrest for the trees. AGAIN! NO ONE IS AKING YOU FOR MONEY! IT HAS BEEN VOLUNTARY FROM THE BEGINING! SEGIRL, GTBASTARD, BLACK. YOU HAD YOUR SAY NOW SHUT UP ABOUT IT, IT'S OVER!!! JESUS CHRIST! HOW MANY TIMES DO YOU DUNDER HEADS HAVE TO HAVE IT SAID? IF YOU DON'T LIKE IT SKIP IT! Now, I want SEgirl to give one example of someone flat out begging for money. I can see why people avoid this place. It's the stupid ones that irritate you. Also, I wan't all of those who have a complaint about the way this or any other post I have made, in regard to asking for money, to give an example of how I asked you or any one else to donate, or how I pressured anyone or how I begged anyone, or how any of this is ILLEAGLE!!!   <p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 02-08-2001).]||||reg||8
