Z||000037||TheFiero64||02-08-2001||10:33 AM||||I almost didn't post as I wanted to stay away from the tension. I always try to look at both sides of everything and figure out the best intelligent option. I thought it out and my Idea is: If you don't like what is going on in a certain topic than don't post to it <B>PERIOD!</B> I hate to see anyone get upset over something when they can just click back in there browser and forget that thread. I think of PFF as family and hate to see a family dispute over this topic. <P><BR>P.S. Welcome 84SEgirl. My GF jaygee79 on the forum has an 84SE and 84SEgirl is also one of her aol screen names.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||4
Z||000038||Gold-86SE||02-08-2001||10:44 AM||||<BR>Ok folks.  I'm steppin' into the middle of this quagmire.  I was one of those who originally mentioned the idea of another Fiero.<P>It is in this thread <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005057.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005057.html</A>  - the last post of the first page.<P>Before I progress, let me review.  This whole thing began when someone reported the accident and then someone mentioned sending flowers from PFF giving our condolenences.<P>Then I stated the following:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>I have a thought, give me your feedback.<P>If this guy still wants a Fiero after this nasty spill, and if his insurance company doesn't provide much help, let's see what we can do to help locate a Fiero that would put him into approximately the same Fiero he lost.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This statements says, if he does not have any insurance to help with the replacement of his vehicle, let's see what we can do to help FIND a Fiero - not purchase one for him.  From this one, small statement it blossomed into the fund we know today.<P>Do I have a problem with this? No.  Those who responded to the original thread were optimistic and felt for the guy - I mean look at that photo, who could not feel for him.<P>To date, I have not sent money to the fund for my own reasons, yet we still do not know if he has collision coverage on his Fiero, or if the other driver's insurance company has paid for Anothony's destroyed Fiero.  My statement was a feeler for those watching the happenings with the thread.<P>If you don't like the idea of some of us seeing if there is something we can do, then don't participate.  Many things occur on this forum that I don't necessarily agree with but, I keep my mouth shut. Why? Because what they are discussing does not really affect me in any way.<P>I almost since a tad bit of jealousy(sp) regarding this situation.  And that my Fiero loving family is sad.  We have had a pretty tight group and identity going and I have been willing to spread the news about PFF, but this type of stuff is non-sense.<P>If a few people cannot post ideas and receive supporters for there ideas, the why do we even have this forum.  Thanks to the good graces of Cliff, we have a place were a lot of Fiero lovers can meet.  And, with that comes the realization that we all have different ideas and thoughts.  Hence, we should be respectful of all opinions and thoughts.<P>I still want to help Anthony, but I would like more information regarding the status of the accident claim.  Who has paid? Was the Fiero replaced? etc.<P>I am disappointed in this negative attitude toward such a in-the-making process.  Other than starting the fund to help Anthony, if he needs the help, nothing, NOTHING, has been done.<P>BTW, has anyone spoken with Anthony?  How is he doing?<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)<BR>Please visit my <A HREF="http://www.trifocus.net/~fws/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Work Shop</A>||||reg||1
Z||000039||GT Bastard||02-08-2001||10:54 AM||||Out of respect for Cliff and the forum, I'll refrain from stooping to Bam-Bams level.||||reg||13
